	# Starsector Marines i18n namespace.
	#
	# Translators: copy this file into a translation mod, change the values
	# (NOT the keys), and load it after Starsector Marines in your mod list —
	# Starsector merges later JSONs on top.

	"marineOps": {
    "openingYardHeading": "SECOND WIND / PLANETARY YARD",
    "openingYardReceipt": "WORK ACCEPTED",
    "openingYardHomeTitle": "ROOM TO LIVE",
    "openingYardOrderTitle": "THE WORK WE CAN AFFORD",
    "openingYardSurveyTitle": "WHAT HELD TOGETHER",
    "openingYardAfterCaption": "After conversion / new bunks, old scars, sealed compartments",
    "openingYardEstimateCaption": "Second Wind under inspection / the rest of the restoration must wait",
    "openingYardBeforeCaption": "Before conversion / sleeping between the cargo lashings",
    "openingYardHomeNarrative": "The cargo lashings have gone from the port-side sleeping space. Steel bunks stand in their place, with lockers bolted underneath and pressure-tested seams around them. Someone has already put a pair of boots under a rack. Across the passage, the barred hatch has not moved. Through its inspection glass you can still see the collapsed machinery.",
    "openingYardOrderNarrative": "The estimate trades twenty-five units of cargo space for eighteen additional personnel places and a permanent company command fit. It pays for usable quarters and the conversion, not a complete restoration. The second boat bay, main machine shop, mess, spare bunkrooms and Mech Lab remain damaged. Both Hermes still need work. No boat or mech comes with this order.",
    "openingYardSurveyNarrative": "Under the yard lamps, the patches that carried you out of the Claim look painfully small. Scorched plating surrounds borrowed seals; a bent rib has been shored with a length of cargo rail. Your people have been living in whichever compartments still hold pressure. Beyond the barred hatches are rooms you have only seen by inspection lamp.",
    "openingYardHomeDialogue": "First thing Sabine asked was whether her people could leave their bedding out. Didn't ask about the command fit. Just wanted to know if somebody would need that patch of deck for cargo tomorrow. I told her those racks were theirs.\n\nWe're still eating field rations, and the shop, mess, spare quarters and second bay are still shut. The Mech Lab is a wreck too. I've put the rest of the survey in Engineering. When the work starts paying, we'll bring her back a room at a time.",
    "openingYardSurveyDialogue": "We made her fly with what the Claim left us. That got everyone out. It didn't make her somewhere a company could live. This order gives Sabine's people bunks of their own and puts the command fit in properly. The sealed rooms stay sealed. We can't afford to open every hatch just because we've finally found a yard.",
    "openingYardCashDialogue": "The estimate still stands. This one comes out of the ship's account, so look at what's left before you sign. The rest of the restoration can wait until we have work.",
    "openingYardConversionFacts": "Permanent conversion: +18 personnel capacity / -25 cargo capacity",
    "openingYardPaid": "Conversion paid and installed / no boats, mechs or further room repairs included",
    "openingYardBill": "Cost: 5,000 credits\nReserved payment: {0} / Due from fleet: {1}\nAvailable fleet credits: {2} / Short by: {3}",
    "openingYardShip": "Vessel: {0}",
    "openingYardEngineeringNote": "Engineering retains the outstanding condition survey.",
    "openingYardReviewNote": "Inspection and review spend nothing. Installation is a permanent yard order.",
    "openingYardInstall": "Install conversion",
    "openingYardReview": "Review yard order",
    "shepherdSalvageSchedules": "Mara says you're the company that found out who was selling Wayline's schedules.",
    "shepherdSalvageWeWere": "We were.",
    "shepherdSalvageCareful": "Then you'll understand why I'm careful what I say in front of Wayline's people.",
    "shepherdSalvageNotWayline": "We're not Wayline's people. We took their contract. Now we'd be taking yours.",
    "shepherdSalvageWreckfall": "We'll see. You've read the survey, so you've seen the valley. Here's the rest. Three cycles back, two fleets fought it out in low orbit over Asharu. A Colossus and a few of her escorts came down here. We were the first crew in. The claim's ours.",
    "shepherdSalvageLongTime": "Three cycles is a long time on one wreck.",
    "shepherdSalvageCamp": "It's a Colossus. You don't strip one in a season. That fight dropped hulls from here to the southern flats, so every crew on Asharu had its own pickings and nobody bothered with us. Then word got round we'd found something.",
    "shepherdSalvageWordQuestion": "Got round how?",
    "shepherdSalvageFuelOrder": "When we opened the hold, I put in a fuel order with Wayline. Enough to lift something heavy off-world, and a camp like ours never needs that much. A few weeks later Dace Harlan's crew came in shooting at shift change.",
    "shepherdSalvageSchedulesSold": "That's about when Wayline's schedules were being sold.",
    "shepherdSalvageOccupation": "You'd know better than I would. Or it was me, talking too loud in a Jangala bar. I can't prove either. We got most of our people out, and now the roaches are stripping our yard and telling anyone who'll listen it was abandoned.",
    "shepherdSalvageSurvivors": "Most of your people.",
    "shepherdSalvageCousin": "My cousin Jory's crew is still inside the Colossus, sealed in where the squatters haven't found a way through. They've kept a quiet channel open. That's how I know the yard's held, and roughly by how many.",
    "shepherdSalvagePermitQuestion": "This is Hegemony space. Is anyone else going to take an interest?",
    "shepherdSalvagePermit": "Our permit's on file at Jangala. The Hegemony doesn't send a patrol over two salvage crews squabbling in a ditch. It'd come quick enough if somebody gave it a reason. So we settle this ourselves, and quietly.",
    "shepherdSalvageScopeQuestion": "Then tell me where it ends. We're not going into your Colossus, and we're not chasing this outfit across Asharu.",
    "shepherdSalvageHandlers": "Good. I don't want you in her, and Jory's people will keep out of your way. You take the receiving store and the workshop; my militia follow you in and hold them. Then the service cradle.",
    "shepherdSalvageCradleQuestion": "What's on the cradle?",
    "shepherdSalvageShepherd": "A Shepherd. Another hull off that fight. Broke her back coming down; we hauled her in to cut up. Her reactor and drone bay are the best scrap in this yard outside the Colossus, and I had a buyer asking after that bay before any of this. Jory says they've had her panels off for a week.",
    "shepherdSalvageOrders": "I want to know what they've taken. Two of my techs on her, with your rifles round them, long enough to find out. Cover them from her south side. Harlan's lot come and go along the south haul road. That's where they'll come back.",
    "shepherdColdRepairTerms": "Wayline's finally dropped the distribution rig on the receiving apron. My fitters take it to the workshop, bring the pump station back and put shore power into the yard. You keep them breathing while they do it. Then you're done.",
    "shepherdColdRoadsQuestion": "And the roads?",
    "shepherdColdCheckpoints": "Checkpoints on the south haul and the quarry road, manned by day hands from the camps down the valley. My own militia hold the inner line.",
    "shepherdColdDayHands": "Day hands.",
    "shepherdColdCheap": "Armed, paid, and a third of what you cost.",
    "shepherdColdCheckpointWorth": "Harlan's crew took this yard off your own people. They'll know what a checkpoint is worth.",
    "shepherdColdPastQuarry": "Harlan's past the quarry. Jory's watched for three days and they haven't come near.",
    "shepherdColdBuildersQuestion": "Your techs said Harlan's crew were trying to wake Morrow's bay. Did anyone ask why?",
    "shepherdColdBuilders": "Teo thinks her builders could put guns up round the yard. Maybe they could. That bay's the most saleable thing I own outside the Colossus, and every hour those drones work is wear on it. I'm not burning it on guns I don't need.",
    "shepherdColdCompanyCover": "Your yard. Captain, we cover the rig and the pump, and when the lights come on we lift.",
    "shepherdColdPickets": "Keep fire off my fitters. And if those checkpoints call for help, they're on my payroll. Cover them back to the inner line.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation1": "My haulers are loaded and going nowhere. The roaches have dug in on the outer road, and two nights ago another crew's boat came down at the quarry.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation2": "So they're waiting for your shipment to move.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation3": "They're waiting for it to move without you beside it. I need the road opened to the eastern yard, with positions along it my militia can hold after you've gone.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation4": "Positions built by what?",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation5": "By Morrow. Teo and the fitters have her lift working. She'll hover. She can crawl the road behind you and put her builders down wherever you've cleared.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation6": "That's a bigger job than the yard. What does it pay?",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation7": "A share when the shipment sells.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation8": "When it sells. To a buyer we don't know, for cargo you won't describe, out past a crew that's already shown it'll kill for it.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation9": "You've had every credit I owed you, on time. Wayline hasn't, so you can guess who I paid first.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation10": "We have, and I'd like it to stay that way. Our payroll doesn't wait on your buyer.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation11": "Then what do you want?",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation12": "Morrow.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation13": "No.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation14": "She's the best thing in this yard that isn't in the Colossus. Her bay was meant to carry this camp through the season, and now she flies, she's worth three times that.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation15": "Who are you going to sell her to?",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation16": "That's my business.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation17": "Whoever buys a flying Shepherd has to register her at a Hegemony port. Somebody asks where she came from. Then somebody asks what else came down in this valley.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation18": "Is that a threat?",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation19": "It's a reason. We've no interest in telling anyone anything. A mercenary company coming out of a wreck field with a recovered hull is nobody's news. It's how we got our first ship.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation20": "Take her for the job, then. Bring her back when the road's done, and I'll pay you out of the shipment on top.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation21": "That's the same promise with a ship attached.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation22": "Then hear mine. You get the hull and nothing else. Every spare we've already pulled off her stays here. The guns she builds stay here. Not a credit for the road, and not a bolt out of the Colossus.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation23": "Agreed.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation24": "And she's not yours until the road's handed to my militia and she's clear of this basin. You don't lift while my people are still walking into position.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation25": "They'll have cover all the way up. We hand over each position before we move on. Who's flying her?",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation26": "Your own people. Nobody from Basin goes with her. Not Teo, not anyone.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation27": "I wasn't going to ask.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation28": "Good. Teo will walk your crew through her before the drive test. Then he comes home.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation29": "We'll put a crew across from Second Wind. Both ships will be running thin until we can hire. Send the terms and I'll put it to the Captain.",
    "shepherdPassageNegotiation30": "I'll send them. Get her out in one piece, Castle. I've watched enough ships come down in this valley.",
    "shepherdPassageInstructions": "Morrow's holding a hover. Bring her along the road to the eastern yard. Clear the pump bend and use Build Vulcan Turret on ground her builders can reach, then do the same at the narrows. Cover the work and wait for my militia to take over. Keep the company with her for the drive test. If the drives give out, break off and we'll recover her. The deal stands either way.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartSouthHaulContact": "South haul checkpoint's taking fire. They're day hands, Captain, but they're my hire. Give them a hand if you can.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartSouthHaulWithdrawing": "South haul checkpoint's running. Can't say I blame them, for what I'm paying. Cover them back to the inner line.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartSouthHaulOverrun": "South haul checkpoint's gone. So much for proper guards. Watch for anyone coming back, and keep that approach covered.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartSouthHaulInnerHold": "The south haul hands have made the inner line. They're staying put, at least. Help them hold it.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartQuarryContact": "Quarry checkpoint has contact. There's only three of them out there, Captain. Support them if you can.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartQuarryWithdrawing": "Quarry checkpoint's falling back. Keep the crossing covered for them.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartQuarryOverrun": "The quarry checkpoint's gone. Keep the inner line covered. There may still be people coming in.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartQuarryInnerHold": "The quarry hands are in, on the inner line with my militia. Keep that ground covered.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartInnerLineFortified": "The new gun's covering the inner line. Keep the fitters working, Captain. We've bought them some room.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartSouthEntryDenied": "That party on the south haul road has broken off at your screen. Keep watching the entry.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartQuarryEntryDenied": "They've broken off at your quarry-road screen. Don't leave the entry open.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageNarrows": "There's a gun at the pump bend now. Keep that position covered while you move through the narrows. The haulers will need this road behind you.",
    "shepherdPassageClimbOut": "The position's ready. Keep the narrows covered and clear the eastern yard for her drive test. Give her room to leave.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageSpool": "She's in the eastern yard. Your crew are spooling her drives, and Teo's talking them through it. Stay with her, Captain; keep the approach clear.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageFailed": "Abort the departure. Pull back, Captain. I'll get Morrow recovered. The deal stands; we'll have to try the road again.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageCompanyLost": "There's not enough of your company left to cover her. Break off. I'll get her recovered. The deal stands.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageBuildersLost": "Morrow's out of builders. We can't finish the road with this wing. Break off; we'll recover her and fit another.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageRoadTeam0": "Watch the south haul approach while the builders work at the bend, Captain.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageRoadTeam1": "Keep someone on the quarry road while you clear the narrows. That's where the new crew came down.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageRoadTeam2": "Don't leave the pump road open behind you, Captain. We still need that position.",
    "shepherdRadioPassageRoadTeam3": "Hold the last approach. Morrow needs that yard clear until she's away.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartCompanyLost": "Your company can't cover the work any longer. Break off. We'll pick up from whatever's finished.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartBuildersLost": "No builders left to finish the gun. Break off, Captain. The delivery and the power work will keep.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartConvoyArrived": "The rig's on the apron, Captain. Stay with it along the workshop road. I paid for every bolt of it.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartWorkshop": "Rig's at the workshop. Now clear the pump station for my fitters. They need to reconnect shore power.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartPumpStarted": "They're on the pump connection. Keep that ground covered until they're done.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartComplete": "Workshop's running, and Morrow's bay is drawing steady. That's the job done, Captain. I'll settle your fee.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartCrewLost": "We've lost the repair crew. Pull back, Captain. What they finished stays finished. I'll have to find other hands.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartCarrierLost": "The rig's gone. We can't do this without it. Pull the company back, Captain.",
    "shepherdRadioColdStartApproach": "That's not a probe. Harlan's coming for the yard. Castle, I know you were about to lift. Stay. Keep them off my fitters, and watch any drones that are out. They won't stand up to gunfire.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageArrival": "You're down, Captain. Receiving store first, then the workshop. My militia are behind you. Leave the Colossus to us.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageWorkshop": "Receiving store's secure. Workshop next, Captain. Watch the gaps between those salvage stacks.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageCradle": "Workshop's ours. The cradle's just past it. Clear the ground on Morrow's south side for my techs, and keep it clear.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageHull": "There's the Shepherd. Morrow, by her hull plate. Panels open all down her flank; somebody's been busy. Let's see what's left in her.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageRoad": "Captain, keep an eye on the south haul road. It's their way back in. Don't pull cover off the techs to chase them.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageInspection": "South side's clear. My techs are crossing now. Stay close enough to cover them while they work.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageContested": "Hostiles at the cradle. The techs have stopped work. Clear them some room, Captain.",
    "shepherdSalvageSecured": "They're done. Her bay's still in her, and the squatters had cable run into it. They weren't cutting her up, Captain. They were trying to wake her. Your fee's released.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageFailed": "We've lost the inspection party, Captain. Pull back. Nothing more gets done here without another crew.",
    "shepherdReferral1": "Castle. Something for when the company's ready, and not before. One of our accounts on Asharu has a problem.",
    "shepherdReferral2": "Wayline has accounts on Asharu now?",
    "shepherdReferral3": "A few. We haul supplies, fuel and heavy machinery out to the salvage crews there, a little under what the other outfits on Jangala charge. It's how you win customers back after a year like ours.",
    "shepherdReferral4": "And this one?",
    "shepherdReferral5": "Basin Reclamation. A salvage crew working a wreck field in the northern canyons. Tamsin Vale runs it. She came to us because we were cheapest, and she counts every credit like it's her last.",
    "shepherdReferral6": "What's gone wrong?",
    "shepherdReferral7": "Another salvage crew walked in with guns and took her yard. Her account's gone quiet, and there's a load of heavy machinery she's already paid for sitting in our shed with nowhere to deliver it.",
    "shepherdReferral8": "So this is Wayline's problem as much as hers.",
    "shepherdReferral9": "At our rates, I can't afford to lose a paying customer. She'd like her yard back. You'd like to be paid. I don't see anyone losing.",
    "shepherdReferral10": "Is she a friend of yours?",
    "shepherdReferral11": "She's a customer. Not a happy one. She'll tell you why herself, if she decides she likes you. The survey's attached. I told her you were good and quiet.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageDescent1": "Vale, while we're on the way down. What did you find in that hold?",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageDescent2": "Salvage. Mine.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageDescent3": "My people are about to be shot at over it. I'd like to know what for.",
    "shepherdRadioSalvageDescent4": "You're being shot at over my yard, my stores and my workshop, and you're paid for every bit of it. Ask Mara whether I settle. The last time that hold went on anybody's paperwork, I got this. I won't do it twice with people Wayline sent me.",
    "shepherdColdRetryUnpowered": "The rig's still at the workshop, but the pump connection isn't finished. I've found another repair party. Cover them while they get shore power in, then we try Morrow's bay for that road gun. Same contract. I've found more day hands for the checkpoints, for whatever that's worth; help them back to the inner line if they have to come in.",
    "shepherdColdRetryPowered": "The rig's at the workshop and shore power's holding, so we pick up from there. Another repair party's ready. Get that road gun out of Morrow's bay and keep the fitters covered. Same contract. I've found more day hands for the checkpoints, for whatever that's worth; help them back to the inner line if they have to come in.",
    "shepherdPassageRetry": "We still have a deal, Castle. Teo needs time on her drives before we try again. I'll see to it, and I'll send fresh holders. Clear the pump bend and the narrows, cover the building, then hand the positions over. Stay with her through the drive test. When the road's ours and she's clear of the basin, she's yours.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageCables": "Payment's received. Why would a salvage crew want a wrecked drone tender awake?",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageStillMine": "Same reason anyone wants builders on a yard they mean to keep, I'd guess. Doesn't matter now. The bay's still in her, and she's still mine.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageFar": "They won't have gone far.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvagePower": "Past the quarry, Jory says, and still going. I've got my yard back and no power to work it. The heavy machinery to fix that is still in Wayline's shed, and they stripped the pump station. Mara can deliver now there's a yard to deliver to. One more contract: cover my fitters while we get the lights on.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageOneMore": "One more?",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageGuards": "After that I've got guards coming for the roads. Nothing personal, Castle. You're good, and you're not cheap.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageReady": "We'll get the company ready. Keep your fitters together until we're there to cover them.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageLosses": "You lost people at that cradle. We'll put ours in order before we take another crew out there.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageApron": "Do. The rig will be on the receiving apron. Come to me when you're ready.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdBuilders": "Captain, did you see how fast those builders put that gun up? Off a wreck we found in pieces.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdWorth": "I saw. Teo had her bay talking before the lights were steady. A Shepherd with a working bay is worth three of her in pieces, so don't look at her like that, Castle. Your fee's sent.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdCheckpoints": "And your checkpoints?",
    "shepherdDebriefColdPaidOff": "Paid off. Most of them have gone home, and I can't say I blame them. Harlan's back on the outer road, and Jory says he's had company since. Finish up with your people, then come and see me. Seems I'm not done with you after all.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdLosses": "We'll need time before we take on anything else. We've people to account for.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdRoadAfterLosses": "So do I. Take it. The outer road's still shut, and I won't talk about that over the radio. Come and see me when you can.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageRegistry": "Registry confirms it, Captain. Morrow's ours. She's flying on a skeleton crew off Second Wind, and Second Wind's not much better off. We'll need to hire before we ask much of either of them.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageFilters": "Have your crew check her drone-bay filters first. Basin dust gets into everything.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageHands": "Any chance of hands from the camp?",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageJangala": "Try the port at Jangala. Nobody in this valley's leaving it for you.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageJory": "Jory's crew can walk out of the Colossus tonight. Safe passage, Castle.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageCompanyLosses": "I know what it cost your people to get her out. I'll leave you to them. Safe passage, Castle.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageMilitiaLosses": "I'd better go. There are families waiting on a call from me, and some of them are mine. Look after her, Castle.",
    "shepherdRewardHeader": "PAYMENT IN KIND",
    "shepherdRewardShip": "Morrow / Shepherd",
    "shepherdRewardHandover": "Road handover and climb-out / Morrow and willing crew join the fleet",

    "shepherdInspectionFacts": " Inspection technicians lost: {0}.",
    "shepherdRepairFacts": " Cargo delivered: {0}. Shore power restored: {1}. Turret constructed this sortie: {2}. Repair technicians lost: {3}.",
    "shepherdPassageLosses": " Cooperative militia lost: {0}.",
    "shepherdPassageTerms": "Road repair, construction and defended militia handover in exchange for Morrow and willing working crew after the hull clears the basin. The cooperative retains the Colossus, its shipment and the yard. No departure cash fee. ",
    "shepherdColdTerms": "22,000 credits for cargo escort and repair cover. Morrow remains cooperative property. ",
    "shepherdSalvageTerms": "18,000 credits for yard clearance and inspection. Cooperative militia hold the outer road; Morrow remains cooperative property. ",
    "shepherdPassageDeployment": "Company boats carry your selected squads. An owned mech is optional. Eight cooperative militia hold the prepared road positions. ",
    "shepherdInspectionDeployment": "Company boats carry your selected squads. An owned mech is optional. Eight cooperative militia and two inspection technicians support the operation. ",
    "shepherdColdDeployment": "Your selected squads begin on the secured receiving apron; company boats stay in reserve. An owned mech is optional. Fourteen cooperative militia support the operation: eight inner holders and two three-person outer pickets. Two technicians accompany the repair party. ",
    "shepherdForceRequirement": "Two squads recommended; two with at least four ready marines each required. ",
    "shepherdColdReplacementParty": "Confirmed repair crew losses: {0}. A replacement party is assigned. ",
    "shepherdColdStatusUnpowered": "Shore power disconnected. ",
    "shepherdColdStatusPowered": "Yard lights and shore power online. ",
    "shepherdColdStatusUndelivered": "Distribution rig awaiting escort. ",
    "shepherdColdStatusDelivered": "Distribution rig delivered. ",
    "shepherdPassageStatus": "Repaired cooperative hull ready for road handover and departure. Confirmed previous militia losses: {0}. Vale supplies new cooperative holders. ",
    "shepherdColdTranscriptTitle": "COLD START / CASTLE & VALE",
    "shepherdPassageTranscriptTitle": "ROAD HANDOVER / CASTLE & VALE",
    "shepherdMissionSalvage": "Salvage Rights",
    "shepherdMissionCold": "Cold Start",
    "shepherdMissionPassage": "Working Passage",
    "shepherdResultSalvageRetry": "No inspection fee awarded. Confirmed company and inspection losses remain on record; Vale will assign a new party for another attempt.",
    "shepherdResultSalvageNextJob": "Morrow remains cooperative property. Cold Start offers paid cargo escort and repair cover when your company is ready.",
    "shepherdResultSalvageSettled": "Inspection contract settled. Payment released; the cooperative yard and inspection are secured. ",
    "shepherdResultSalvageExercise": "Training record only; no campaign inspection milestone or payment is issued. ",
    "shepherdResultSalvageIncomplete": "INSPECTION UNFINISHED / RETRY AVAILABLE",
    "shepherdResultSalvageInspected": "YARD INSPECTION COMPLETE / COOPERATIVE SHIP",
    "shepherdResultColdRetry": "No repair payment awarded. Vale will assign replacement cooperative personnel. Completed delivery and shore power remain on record; unfinished work needs another mobilization.",
    "shepherdResultColdNextJob": "Morrow remains cooperative property. The outer road is no longer held; Working Passage opens a separate negotiation for road repair, construction and militia handover.",
    "shepherdResultColdSettled": "Repair contract settled. Payment released. ",
    "shepherdResultColdExercise": "Training record only; no campaign payment is issued. ",
    "shepherdResultColdIncomplete": "REPAIR MOBILIZATION UNFINISHED",
    "shepherdResultColdRepaired": "REPAIRS COMPLETE / SHIP STILL GROUNDED",
    "shepherdResultPassageRetry": "The road-handover agreement and completed repairs remain. Vale will recover and refit the same grounded hull for another departure; confirmed losses remain on the account.",
    "shepherdResultPassageSettled": "Contract settled. Morrow and a minimum working crew join your fleet as the final payment in kind. The cooperative retains the Colossus, its shipment and the reopened yard. No additional cash payment.",
    "shepherdResultPassageExercise": "Training record only; no fleet transfer.",
    "shepherdResultPassageIncomplete": "DEPARTURE INCOMPLETE",
    "shepherdResultPassageDisabled": "CRITICAL DISABLE / DEPARTURE ABORTED",
    "shepherdResultPassageDeparted": "MORROW / PHYSICAL CLIMB-OUT CONFIRMED",
    "shepherdResultContractRecord": "BASIN RECLAMATION / CONTRACT RECORD",
    "shepherdInspectionTranscriptTitle": "YARD INSPECTION / CASTLE & VALE",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageExerciseRepairParty": "The actual contract includes a repair party. We'd supply the parts and fitters.",
    "shepherdDebriefSalvageExercise": "Inspection exercise complete. No campaign inspection milestone or payment is issued.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdExerciseCosts": "Keep the exercise losses in the review. A contracted company has to cover supplies and crew pay before committing to departure.",
    "shepherdDebriefColdExercise": "Repair exercise complete. No campaign payment is issued.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageExerciseCrew": "A contracted departure would include berth offers to willing working hands. Fleet crew, on our payroll, with the ship's upkeep ours from handover.",
    "shepherdDebriefPassageExerciseTerms": "The contract would leave the Colossus shipment, yard and haul road with us. The company's final payment would be Morrow; this exercise makes no transfer.",
