    "gearCatalogWeaponsAssaultLore": "A Tri-Tachyon-adjacent blacksite package for breaking defended rooms before the enemy can reorganize. Clean Lancer cells provide the line fire; serial-free Rattlers open the breach; a single diverted Shattercap answers massed soft targets without appearing on a corporate manifest.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsAssaultProvenance": "Deniable corporate security",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFieldSecurityLore": "A practical station-security issue for settlements that cannot expect prompt naval help. Twelve ubiquitous Domain-pattern Rooks fill the racks. Specialist weapons are a future technology acquisition, not part of the founding issue.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFieldSecurityProvenance": "Independent frontier",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFireSupportLore": "A low-tech support establishment built to keep firing after a campaign has outlasted its first supply plan. Every team combines the serviceable Rook, a Stalwart automatic, and a Longbow marksman; old Annihilator clusters and tightly controlled Breachlights provide the scarce heavy issue.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsFireSupportProvenance": "Hegemony auxiliary tables",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLineInfantryLore": "League interoperability means agreeing on cells, ammunition, and fire-team roles without pretending every member world owns the same factories. Lancers lead, Rooks and Stalwarts sustain the line, Longbows exploit open lanes, and Wayfarer smoke keeps a stalled advance moving.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLineInfantryProvenance": "Persean League coalition",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLuddicPathAssaultLore": "Recovered Pather assault tables contain no clean quartermaster's mirror of a state arsenal. Blackforge Rattlers, old Rooks, industrial Breachhands, and a scarce captured heavy weapon turn ordinary compartments into close, decisive killing grounds.",
    "gearCatalogWeaponsLuddicPathAssaultProvenance": "Luddic Path",
