    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideOurStoresAreStillReserved": "OUR STORES ARE STILL RESERVED",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideNothingWasSpentByLeavingCommanderOur": "Leaving didn''t cost us anything, Commander. The rest of the shuttle parts and squad stores are waiting at {0}. They''re held ashore, so I can''t draw them from up here. Go back, choose Marine operations in the planet menu, and we''ll pick up where we stopped. Don''t buy them twice.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideReturn": "RETURN",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideReturnToDepot": "RETURN TO DEPOT",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideChooseOurCompanyShip": "CHOOSE OUR COMPANY SHIP",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideCommanderChooseAHomeWithQuartersAnd": "Commander, pick our home: a ship with quarters and a boat bay. These stores cover one shuttle, which can make the trip as often as we need, and kit for one full squad. Sabine''s appointment is settled, first training point and all.\n\n{0}",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideOurCompanyCommandVessel": "OUR COMPANY COMMAND VESSEL",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideMercenaryCompanyConversion": "MERCENARY COMPANY CONVERSION",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideChooseShip": "CHOOSE SHIP",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideAHomeForTheCompany": "A HOME FOR THE COMPANY",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuidePreparingOurShip": "PREPARING OUR SHIP",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideLetSGetTheCompanyReady": "LET'S GET THE COMPANY READY",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideTheCrewIsPreparingOurQuartersAnd": "The crew are clearing our quarters and the hangar. When the deck's ready we commission our lift, sit down with Sabine and muster her squad.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideOurHomeIsReadyComeDownTo": "Home's ready. Come down to the Boat Deck and we'll get our first shuttle flying.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideOurLiftIsAboardComeToBarracks": "Our lift's aboard. Come to Barracks; Sabine's waiting.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideBoatDeck": "BOAT DECK",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideMeetSabine": "MEET SABINE",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideRepairOurFirstHermes": "REPAIR OUR FIRST HERMES",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideCommissionOurFirstShuttle": "COMMISSION OUR FIRST SHUTTLE",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideSecondWindCameWithTwoWreckedHermes": "Second Wind came with two wrecked Hermes. We can reach this one; the other's behind the sealed second bay. Let's patch this one for the first contracts.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideCheckTheMaterialBillThenConfirmThe": " Check the material bill, then confirm the work.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideSelectTheFirstBerthOnTheRight": " Select the first berth on the right.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideOurPrepaidStoresAreAvailableWhileDocked": " Our prepaid stores are available while docked at the conversion planet.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideLiftReady": "LIFT READY",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideGoodThatBoatIsOursWithA": "Good. That boat's ours: a berth on the deck and a bill that's paid. She can make the trip as many times as the squad needs. Plating and drive can wait for money we haven't earned yet. Now, Sabine.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideOneStepAtATime": "ONE STEP AT A TIME",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideWeWillMusterTheSquadOnceOur": "We muster the squad once the ship, the lift and the field commander are ready. Those first.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideContinue": "CONTINUE",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideMusterOurFirstSquad": "MUSTER OUR FIRST SQUAD",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideTwelveMarinesThirtySixSuppliesAndTwenty": "Twelve marines, thirty-six supplies and twenty-four food. That's Sabine's section on the company roll: kitted, fed and paid from today. Check the highlighted bill and choose Found Line Squad; then we hand them back to her.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideAFormationNeedsItsOfficer": "A FORMATION NEEDS ITS OFFICER",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideTheSquadAndItsFieldKitAre": "They're on the roll and kitted. Back to Barracks to give Sabine her standing command. Assigning them costs nothing more.",
    "openingCompanyPreparationGuideBarracks": "BARRACKS",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideAHomeForTheCompany": "A HOME FOR THE COMPANY",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideFirstCommanderChooseAShipWithQuarters": "First, Commander, a ship with quarters and a boat bay. I've counted the stores for our first lift and a full squad. Bring the whole bill aboard before we start, and we'll see this through together.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideOurFirstLift": "OUR FIRST LIFT",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideOurPeopleNeedAWayDownAnd": "Our people need a way down and a way home. Pick an empty berth and commission its shuttle. One boat can ferry the squad in trips; more boats put them down together. Keep the squad's stores aside for the next step.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideMeetYourFieldCommander": "MEET YOUR FIELD COMMANDER",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideCommanderWillLeadOurFirstFormationYou": "Sabine leads our first formation, Commander. She''s been bringing those twelve home since the ore runs; now she does it for us. You set the course, she brings our people through it. Open her portrait on the left. Let''s give her a proper start.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideHerFirstSpecialty": "HER FIRST SPECIALTY",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideSheHasOneTrainingPointCoverProtects": "She has one training point. Cover keeps her troops alive under fire; Recovery Planning gets our wounded back on their feet; Salvage Stewardship brings more home from the field; Field Medicine gives each squad a medic who patches up the wounded in battle. Read all four, then choose. It's permanent. Her next promotion earns another.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuidePeopleBeforeOrders": "PEOPLE BEFORE ORDERS",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideNowSheNeedsAFormationRaiseA": "Now her people need to be ours on paper. Raise a squad in the Armory, then come back here. Twelve marines, thirty-six supplies and twenty-four food buy their field kit and stores. Check the bill, then put their names on the roll.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideGiveHerACommand": "GIVE HER A COMMAND",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideSelectTheSquadThenClickAssignSelected": "Select the squad, then click Assign Selected on {0}''s commander card on the left. Her portrait will appear on the squad. This is her standing formation; you can reorganize it as the company grows.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideACompanyTakingShape": "A COMPANY TAKING SHAPE",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideGoodSheHasASpecialtyAndPeople": "Good. She has a specialty and people to lead. Sabine's word, not mine: \"Twelve present, Commander. Counted. First time anyone's paid them to stand watch since the Claim. Give me somewhere to take them.\" At briefing, put her squad on the mission. Every officer who goes earns their own service record. Bring them home and we'll build on what they learn.",
    "openingOfficerInductionGuideReady": "READY",
    "openingCompanyPrologueAWorkingPlanetarySpaceport": "a working planetary spaceport",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSecondWind": "SECOND WIND",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheWritingOnTheWall": "THE WRITING ON THE WALL",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWhatWeLeftBehind": "WHAT WE LEFT BEHIND",
    "openingCompanyPrologueRaisingHer": "RAISING HER",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheDepartureRoster": "THE DEPARTURE ROSTER",
    "openingCompanyPrologueSomewhereToDock": "SOMEWHERE TO DOCK",
    "openingCompanyPrologueAWayToEarn": "A WAY TO EARN",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheFirstStep": "THE FIRST STEP",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheAlarmAboveTheHatchHasFinally": "The hatch alarm stopped an hour ago. Castle still looks up at it whenever the drive changes pitch. Someone has wedged a folded shift roster under the navigation console to stop it rattling. Harker's Claim is several jumps behind you, and nobody aboard has said its name since the first.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueHarkerSClaimWasThreeWeeksHaul": "Harker's Claim was three weeks' haul from the nearest port, and the transplutonic ore in its seams was worth every day of it. Then the good seams thinned, and slowly the Claim stopped paying. The second shaft was \"suspended pending survey.\" The drill rigs went out on the carriers \"for refurbishment\" and never came back. The clinic lost its surgeon to a transfer nobody had applied for. Carriers came monthly instead of weekly, and left heavier than they arrived. The notice that finally went up in the canteen was two lines long and ended with a date.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheLastOreCarrierTookTheMine": "The date was when facility support would end: air, heat, power. The last ore carrier left eleven days before it, with the administrators and the payroll aboard. Passage for workers was offered, priced in credits nobody paid in scrip could raise. The rest of the Claim kept reporting for shifts until the ration counter stopped taking company scrip.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheCerberusByTheLoadingLocksHad": "The Cerberus by the loading locks had been the Claim's escort hull until the operator decided ore didn't need escorting. For nearly a decade she was a parts bin, tethered at the locks with her shields cold and her point defence stripped, and the belt's small rocks found her one at a time. Someone chalked the days left beside her airlock, and someone else kept the count honest. You took drive coil from a hauler that hadn't flown since before the Claim had a name, pressure seals off the doors of habs nobody would need again, and a navigation core out of the administrator's empty office. Sabine's section unbolted the point-defence mounts from the gantries and carried them aboard by hand. You still have the list of everything you couldn't replace. It is longer than the list of what you could.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheDepartureRosterIsInYourHandwriting": "The departure roster is in your handwriting. Castle's additions run down the margin in a smaller hand: fuel, seals, filters, one more person who needed a berth, then another. Near the bottom, in block capitals, Sabine Hale has added her escort section: fifteen names, two struck through. Nobody held a vote about the command chair. While you were checking the last pressure patch, someone painted SECOND WIND over the old registry and didn't sign it.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCorvusHasWorkingYardsAndRegularTraffic": "Corvus has working yards, steady freight and Hegemony patrols crawling across the navigation display. Castle scrolls past the public yard listings to a private address: Nessa Venn, Jangala. The last message in the thread is years old and ends in the middle of an argument. Castle reads it twice before she starts a new one.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCastleSearchesThePortListingsForSomewhere": "Castle works down the port listings for anywhere that will berth a civilian hull and has a yard that can actually do the work. Half of them want a deposit just to reply. A published berth and a working yard are worth more than anyone's promise.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueACargoHandSleepsBesideTheBridge": "A cargo hand sleeps against the bridge hatch with her boots on. The crew take turns in the bunks that still hold pressure. In the cargo hold, Sabine's twelve sleep in shifts beside their stacked rifles, the way they did on the ore runs. Below decks are two wrecked Hermes and compartments you haven't dared put back on the power bus. Castle has been reading surface security notices: depots, convoy stops, freight roads that need guarding and can't afford anyone established.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueCastlePutsTheYardEstimateBesideThe": "Castle lays the yard estimate on top of the old shift roster. For a moment she holds it flat, her palm over the operator's crest. Then she slides both aside so you can reach the navigation controls.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouCanLetGoOfTheChair": "You can let go of the chair, Commander. She's holding. I sent everyone I could spare to get some sleep. They keep asking me where we're headed, and what happens when we get there. I told them you'd already picked a direction. Don't make a liar of me.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueIRanTheClaimSManifestsForNine": "I ran the Claim's manifests for nine years. Every month they told us output was down, outbound tonnage went up. Spare rigs, reactor stock, the clinic's scanner, all listed as ore. They weren't failing, Commander. They were packing.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueStillHadAMonthSPayOn": "Still had a month''s pay on my account at the Claim. Kept the chit. Couldn''t tell you why. {0}What''s left in the ship''s account is everybody''s. Make it last.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueFourDaysLeftOnTheChalkWhen": "Four days left on the chalk when you lit her drive. I watched the whole loading dock hold its breath. Nobody asked whether she'd fly, Commander. Not once. They asked what to carry next.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueTheRealMoneySMostlySpokenFor": "The real money's spoken for. The yard payment's locked away where nobody can borrow against it, and the shuttle parts and the squad's kit are paid. ",
    "openingCompanyPrologueIVePaidForShuttlePartsAnd": "Shuttle parts and the squad's kit are paid for. The yard money has to come out of what's left. ",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouRememberTheNightTheyShutOff": "Remember the night they cut power to the lower habs? You were down there running cable out of this wreck. That's when people started bringing me their names. Not when we lit the drive. So you can stop looking at me every time somebody says \"Commander.\"",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNoAnswerFromAYardWeCan": "No yard in reach is answering. I'll keep trying. We didn't come all this way to live on emergency power.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNessaVennWeRanOreTogetherBefore": "Nessa Venn. We ran ore together before she settled into the yards on Jangala. Once spent three days towing my dead freighter home and swore she'd cut me loose at every buoy. Never did. She'll have opinions about this ship. Let me talk first.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueHasAWorkingYardIDonT": "{0} has a working yard. I don''t know a soul there. We ask for a berth and a written estimate, and we keep our story short.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueYouSaidWeCouldTakeContractWork": "You said once we were clear we'd take contract work. I've been looking. A proper company carries a Hegemony review-board licence; the fee alone is more than this ship is worth. So we take work from people who can't afford licensed companies either. There are plenty of them. Sabine's people haven't been paid in four months and they still stand watch. One shuttle. One squad on the roll, kitted and fed. Then we see.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueThenWeGetABoatFlyingAnd": "{0}Then we get a boat flying and Sabine''s people aboard her. After that... well. We might actually be a company, Commander.",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWeLlFindABerthThenBunks": "We find a berth. Then bunks, a workshop, and someone who can tell us which of those shuttles is worth saving. ",
    "openingCompanyPrologueNessaSentAnEstimateCalledTheJob": "Nessa sent an estimate. She called the job \"ambitious\" twice, which beats \"scrap.\" Five thousand for the conversion, and she's found room in her stores for ours. ",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWeLlGetTheYardAtTo": "The yard at {0} will do the conversion. Five thousand, if they hold to the estimate. ",
    "openingCompanyPrologueIVeKeptThePaymentSafe": "The payment's safe. ",
    "openingCompanyPrologueWeLlHaveToWatchThatYard": "We'll be watching that yard money. ",
